  "caption": "21 elephants walked across me. Which landmark should tell its story next? 👇\n\nA week after the Brooklyn Bridge opened in 1883, a stampede on its stairs killed twelve people, and many New Yorkers doubted it was safe. In May 1884, circus showman P.T. Barnum marched twenty-one elephants across, with the famous Jumbo at the back, as thousands watched.\n\nEvery landmark has a story like this. Urban Tales plays them as you walk past. Link in bio.\n\n.\n.\n.\n#NewYork #BrooklynBridge #NYC #TravelFacts #UrbanTales"
